error[E0409]: `.len` cannot be applied to `str ! {none}`
  --> mem:///main.lu:10:13
   |
10 |     let n = rest.len
   |             ^^^^ this is `str ! {none}`
   |
   = note: a `!T` is two values, never one, and no operator reads it ([type.row.operand]): a member
     read and a method call read their base as an operator reads its operand, and `?`, `else`
     and `match` are the whole of how a row is handled. Handle it first — `rest?.len`, `(rest
     else "").len` — and read what it yields.
